!!id:"https://tson.io/2026/34/ltr8/http/agent-vm-1.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/34/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/34/m/core.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/34/ltr8/http/agent-1.tn"
@doc:"""
  TSON Agent VM — the resolved form of an agent plan
  (draft 2, brought to 2026 Revision 34; companion to agent-1.tn, whose `name` and `constant` it imports).

  An agent is what a plan compiles to: the plan reading's resolved
  output, as a resolved schema is to its source. Compilation is
  deterministic and canonical — pool entries intern in first-use
  order, one memory slot per step in document order — so one plan
  yields one agent and content addressing composes: a server MAY
  accept a plan (compile, verify, execute, cache the agent under the
  plan's hash) or an agent directly (resolution and budgets are
  precomputed; admission re-checks them). Verification is one
  forward pass in both cases: straight-line code has no merge
  points, so checking and inference coincide; type transitions
  against the pinned interface are always the server's work.

  Execution model: a value stack bounded by `max_stack`; write-once
  memory of `slots` slots, assigned in order by STORE; instructions
  execute in sequence; no jumps. Selection instructions are
  absence-absorbing: if the operand consumed is the absent
  sentinel, the result is the absent sentinel. Unhandled call
  failure aborts with agent_error (agent-1.tn), reported in source
  terms via `debug`.
  """
{
  @doc:"Index into `agent.pool`. Varint-friendly in the binary form."
  pool_index => uint32

  @doc:"Index into agent memory; slots are assigned by STORE in order."
  slot_index => uint32

  @doc:"""
    Operand-free operations. Stack effects:
    STORE ( a -- )   pop, assign next free slot
    RET   ( a -- )   the popped value is the agent's response; MUST
                     be the final instruction, reached at depth 1
    """
  simple_op => !enum [STORE RET]

  @doc:"""
    CALL payload. `method` MUST index a `method` pool entry; `or`,
    when present, indexes a `value` entry validated at admission
    against the method's response type — on call failure it replaces
    the response (the lowering of agent.tn's @or). A CALL without
    `or` that fails aborts the plan.
    """
  call_op => {
    method: pool_index
    or:     pool_index?
  }

  @doc:"""
    FILTER payload: pop an array, push the elements whose field
    `field` equals pool value `value` — total, empty in, empty out.
    `field` MUST index a `name` entry declared by the element type;
    `value` MUST index a `value` entry conforming to that field's
    type; equality is over value spaces.
    """
  filter_op => {
    field: pool_index
    value: pool_index
  }

  @doc:"""
    Operand-bearing operations, one label per mnemonic; exactly one
    is present (REQUIRED field group). Stack effects:
    const k  ( -- pool[k] )      k MUST be a `value` entry
    load s   ( -- memory[s] )    s MUST be already assigned
    get f    ( a -- a.f )        field selection; f MUST be a `name`
                                 entry; absence-absorbing
    index n  ( a -- a[n] )       element selection; total where the
                                 source floor proves n, else out of
                                 bounds yields the absent sentinel
    filter p ( a -- a' )         see filter_op
    make t   ( -- {} )           empty instance of `type` entry t,
                                 fields unbound
    set f    ( r v -- r' )       bind field f of record r to v
    pack n   ( a1 .. an -- [a1 .. an] )
    call c   ( req -- resp )     see call_op; req MUST be complete:
                                 every REQUIRED field bound,
                                 defaults injected
    """
  op => {
    ( const:  pool_index
    | load:   slot_index
    | get:    pool_index
    | index:  uint32
    | filter: filter_op
    | make:   pool_index
    | set:    pool_index
    | pack:   uint8
    | call:   call_op )
  }

  @doc:"""
    One instruction: a bare mnemonic or a labelled operand record —
    two discrimination classes, so the choice is tag-free.
    """
  @disjoint
  instruction => ( simple_op | op )

  @doc:"""
    One constant-pool entry. Kinds are explicit so every index is
    kind-checked at admission: `name` for GET/SET/FILTER fields,
    `value` for CONST, FILTER constants, and @or substitutes,
    `type` for MAKE (a request/response type in the interface's
    schema), `method` for CALL.
    """
  pool_entry => {
    ( name:   name
    | value:  constant
    | type:   name
    | method: name )
  }

  @doc:"""
    A compiled agent. Admission, in order: resolve `interface`
    (pin-checked) and its schema chain; kind-check every pool
    index; run the forward pass — per-instruction type transitions,
    selection through OPTIONAL positions only where the target
    admits absence, request completeness at each CALL, declared
    `max_stack` and `slots` exact, RET final at depth 1. The RET
    operand's inferred type is the derived response contract, known
    before execution. `debug` maps memory slots to source step
    names for agent_error reporting.
    """
  agent => {
    version:    uint8 = 2
    interface:  uri
    pool:       [pool_entry; 1..]
    max_stack:  uint16
    slots:      uint16
    code:       [instruction; 1..]
    debug:      {slot_index => name}?
  }
}
